Licensing of the bdhs package and of the data it bundles
=========================================================

The bdhs package combines original code with data from third parties. The
code and the data are licensed separately, as set out below.

1. Package code
---------------
All R code, documentation, data-raw build scripts and the harmonization rules
(inst/extdata/crosswalk.rds, built from data-raw/inputs/crosswalk.json) are
Copyright (c) 2026 Arman Hossen and released under the MIT licence
(see LICENSE and LICENSE.md).

2. DHS Program Indicator Data API (aggregate statistics and catalogues)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files: data/bdhs_indicators.rda, data/bdhs_indicator_catalog.rda,
       data/bdhs_surveys.rda, data/bdhs_datasets.rda

These are official aggregate statistics (indicator values, denominators and
confidence intervals) and metadata (indicator definitions, survey and dataset
catalogues) published by The DHS Program, ICF, through its public Indicator
Data API. They are redistributed unchanged in content (reshaped, exact
duplicate rows removed) for convenience, with citation, and remain the work
of The DHS Program/ICF. They contain no respondent-level data. Retrieved on
2026-10-26 (API version 8.1). Cite as:

  The DHS Program Indicator Data API, The Demographic and Health Surveys
  (DHS) Program. ICF. Originally funded by the United States Agency for
  International Development (USAID). Available from api.dhsprogram.com.
  [Accessed 2026-10-26]

and cite the survey final reports (bdhs_surveys$report_url) when using the
values of a survey.

3. Subnational boundaries (DHS Spatial Data Repository)
--------------------------------------------------------
File: inst/extdata/bdhs_boundaries.rds

Survey-specific subnational boundaries of the Bangladesh surveys from the DHS
Spatial Data Repository, made available under the Open Database License
(ODbL) 1.0 <https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/> for the database
and the Database Contents License (DbCL) 1.0
<https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/> for its contents. The
bundled file is a derived database: duplicated features removed, region codes
of the 2017-18 survey corrected to the microdata coding, geometry simplified
(topology preserving, 100 m tolerance) and attributes added by the bdhs build
scripts (data-raw/boundaries/). It is distributed under the same ODbL 1.0 /
DbCL 1.0 terms. Cite as:

  Spatial Data Repository, The DHS Program, ICF International,
  spatialdata.dhsprogram.com [Accessed 2026-10-26]

4. Codebooks (metadata only)
----------------------------
Files: data/bdhs_codebook.rda, data/bdhs_value_labels.rda

Variable names, variable labels, value labels and per-variable counts of
non-missing values, extracted from DHS recode files that the maintainer is
licensed to use. They describe the structure of the files and contain no
respondent-level values, ranges or frequencies. The labels are the work of
The DHS Program/ICF and the survey implementing agencies.

5. Derived tables
-----------------
data/bdhs_regions.rda is derived from items 3 and 4 and from the bdhs
harmonization rules; data/bdhs_pool_population.rda combines sample sizes from
item 2 with population estimates from

  United Nations, Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population
  Division (2024). World Population Prospects 2024.
  <https://population.un.org/wpp/>, licensed under CC BY 3.0 IGO.

6. No microdata
---------------
The DHS Program licenses survey microdata (respondent-level data) to
registered users only and does not permit its redistribution. bdhs does NOT
contain or distribute any DHS microdata. Users must register at
<https://dhsprogram.com/data/new-user-registration.cfm>, request access to the
Bangladesh surveys and download the files themselves.
